            "review_title": "Review at Com GA Hai Nam",
            "review_text": "David W\nCHAPEL HILL5 contributions\n0\nDelicious, low-cost vittles and good wait-staff.\nMar 2015 • Solo\nMy guest house happens to be in close proximity to one of these franchises, if that's what they are called in Vn. I have seen two others walking out and about.\n\nFor convenience and a good, low price, it's hard to beat this joint. Unless you are willing to patronize the typical HCMCity open street cafes with the kindergarten chairs and tables, or buy food from street vendors (not my cup of tea generally, due to their very low cleanliness and food-prep standards) then you would be hard-pressed to do much better than this Singapore Hainamese nugget of a place.\n\nI did not rate this as an \"excellent\" because I would honestly reserve that for a fancier joint when I want to drop more cash. \"Very Good\" however, due to the immense \"bang for the buck\" virtue.\n\nSure, you can spend plenty more in nicer places with much more classy settings, but for everyday lunch and also dinner, you may want to check this place out if it's convenient.\n\nOne really nice aspect that many similar restaurants do not accommodate is a number of fresh, healthy vegetables steamed or sauteed by themselves, or together with other meats, if desired.\n\nThe grilled meats are especially savory and tender; the service tends to be very quick. The first time I ate, I barely had a chance to order and browse the menu a bit longer before my total dinner order was placed on my table, no joke.\n\nAs always in Vn, at least to an American point of view, the servings tend to be small, but on one occasion, I ordered extra chicken a la carte three times (three leg/thigh portions) in one meal, just to fill me up. There was no upcharge for the rice I did not want, they just charged for the extra meat. Beautiful!\n\nAdded bonus: They have medium to regular adult-sized tables and chairs, much more comfortable to a guy like me at 6 feet, 200#.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 16, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
